WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:05:45.229 --> 00:05:49.140
Who is Tony Stark’s new AI Friday (voiced
by Kerry Condon) she plays Mike’s daughter

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:54.180
in law on Better Call Saul. The FRiday character
debuted During the Iron Man Protocols storyline

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:59.239
in 2009. Pepper Potts stopped being Tony Stark’s
secretary, and instead of hiring a new one,

00:05:59.239 --> 00:06:01.400
he decided to create one. His own Girl Friday.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:06.160
The name is a play on the 1940s Cary Grant
movie called His Girl Friday where he plays

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.589
a newspaper editor trying to keep his ex-wife
from re-marrying because he’s still in love

00:06:08.589 --> 00:06:08.740
with her.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:12.449
So you get the joke. You could make all kinds
of shipping jokes about Tony being in love

00:06:12.449 --> 00:06:19.080
with his AIs like JARVIS. In the comics it
was a pepper potts joke, But the movie turns

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:21.020
it into part of this larger Jocasta Easter
Egg.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.330
Jocasta is His Girl Friday who Tony Stark
is trying to keep from marrying Ultron.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:28.610
In the comics Ultron creates a new AI called
Jocasta to be his perfect Bride. The character

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:31.600
Jocasta is named after the greek tragedy of
Oedipus. The guy that ended up marrying his

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:35.520
mother, there are many levels to this. Which
is why Joss Whedon and Comic Book writers

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:36.990
are so much fun to follow.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:39.550
Ultron built Jocasta using the brain patterns
of the Wasp, Janet Van Dyne. Ultron named

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:40.330
her Jocasta after the wife of Oediups because
Janet Van Dyne was kind of his mother. In

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.339
the comics, Ultron was created by Hank Pym
who was married to Janet Van Dyne. So Ultron

00:06:43.339 --> 00:06:44.570
created his bride in his mother’s image.
Yikes.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:48.079
Just like with Vision turning against Ultron,
Jocasta did too and she joined the Avengers.

00:06:48.079 --> 00:06:54.359
I might have to do a bonus video for her at
some point because she has her own wierd history

00:06:54.359 --> 00:06:54.919
in the comics.

00:06:54.919 --> 00:06:59.770
There was even a time when Jarvis caught her
kissing hank pym in mighty avengers. That

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:03.950
was the storyline where Ultron takes over
Tony Stark’s extremis armor and creates

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.139
a female body for himself.

00:07:05.139 --> 00:07:06.529
I know you guys are wondering if they’d
ever do Jocasta in the movies. It’s possible

00:07:06.529 --> 00:07:10.310
Ultron will be back in some form for Infinity
War, but I’m not expecting it. Think about

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.160
how long the Red Skull has been MIA.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.410
Who are the new characters?

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.829
Helen Cho is a character created by Greg Pak.
The same Greg Pak that wrote Planet Hulk.

00:07:16.829 --> 00:07:19.959
She debuted in Incredible Hercules and was
the mother of Amadeus Cho. In the comics,

00:07:19.959 --> 00:07:24.410
she existed only to serve the development
of the Amadeus Cho character. She was killed

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:29.919
off pretty quickly after Amadeus started partnering
up with Hercules. So the movie is changing

00:07:29.919 --> 00:07:30.870
her backstory.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:35.669
Because she’s so young in the movie, if
they do bring Amadeus Cho into the MCU, it

00:07:35.669 --> 00:07:37.719
would have to be as her brother.

00:07:37.719 --> 00:07:41.679
She’s in love with Thor in the movie, so
wouldn’t it be crazy if Amadeus Cho became

00:07:41.679 --> 00:07:42.919
the son of Thor and Helen Cho?

00:07:42.919 --> 00:07:49.919
The movie kind of gives her some aspects of
the Amadeus character. In the comics, Amadeus

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:57.410
is the 7th smartest person on the planet.
In the movie, Helen Cho is a genius biochemical

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:03.620
engineer that creates the synthetic skin Ultron
uses to 3D print Vision.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:09.830
I’ll explain the Vibranium before I explain
Ulysses Klaw. They kind of go hand in Black

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:10.020
Panther hand.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:12.620
Ultron bonds the Vibranium molecules with
Helen Cho’s synthetic skin technology to

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:18.180
form Vision’s body. The frisbee joke was
so good. The Most versatile substance on earth,

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:25.180
and the humans use it to make a frisbee. Talking
about Captain America’s shield.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:30.800
The reason Vision is able to alter his form
is because he can control the bonded vibranium

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.100
synthetic skin can be reprogrammed as he sees
fit.

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:40.100
As for the flying, they don’t fully explain
how his repulsor technology works in the movie.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:46.600
But blanket movie logic explanation is that
the vibranium based technology is a more advanced

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:51.490
form of Stark Tech. So think of Vision as
a hyper advanced Iron Man suit combined with

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:53.180
AI.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:58.120
The mind gem is the reason he has a soul.
Even though you’d think it would be the

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:59.320
soul gem to do that.

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.900
His consciousness is built on the framework
of Ultron’s Chitauri programming combined

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:03.530
with JARVIS and the Mind Gem.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:07.110
So if they removed the Mind Gem, it might
kill him. He’d probably start acting more

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:12.280
like Ultron. Which might end up happening
when Thanos eventually takes the gem to form

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.620
the infinity gauntlet.

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:20.050
I already did a video explaining a lot of
the Vision’s backstory in my TOP 5 Ultron

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:25.400
stories video. So I’ll add a link to that
in the description.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:28.870
Fun Times with Vibranium Life Forms. Now Ulysses
Klaw, huge Black Panther villain. Andy Serkis,

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:35.460
most definitely going to reappear in the Black
Panther solo film.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:42.460
The movie kind of tells the origin story of
Ulysses Klaw in the comics. He tries to steal

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:49.510
a bunch of Wakanda’s vibranium. Gets away
with a little, but winds up being branded

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:56.490
as a thief and mortal enemy of their people.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:01.780
That’s what the tattoo was. Thats part of
Klaw’s origin story, so if you picked up

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:08.780
the John Romita Jr 2005 Black Panther title.
You can read that story. That’s one way

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.340
in which Marvel is getting rid of origin stories
in the movies.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:21.340
So when we get to the black panther solo film.
They won’t have to explain Klaw’s entire

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:26.560
life history.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:31.110
In the comics he has a mechanical hand. In
the movie Ultron gives him billions of dollars

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:38.110
for the vibranium, then cuts his hand off.
So Klaw has the resources to make himself

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:49.410
a new hand. Probably out of vibranium. That
we’ll probably get to see in the Black Panther

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:05.800
movie.

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:12.800
Doctor List we met on Agents of SHIELD this
week. He’s one of the current heads of HYDRA,

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:20.360
even though he winds up dead along with Baron
Von Strucker.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:30.200
The next big head of HYDRA we’ll probably
meet is Baron Zemo in Captain America Civil

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:50.370
War. HYDRA has been getting the shit kicked
out of it for the last year, but they’re

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:16.870
still very much a thing in

00:12:29.739 --> 00:12:30.310
the movies.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:37.310
Hawkeye and Hulk’s role in the film are
at odds. Their story addresses one of the

00:12:38.489 --> 00:12:45.489
moral cores of the film. Do Avengers get to
have normal lives? Bruce has that line where

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:57.360
he says, I don’t get to have this, talking
about Hawkeye’s secret but suprisingly normal

00:12:57.829 --> 00:13:04.829
family. Hawkeye returns to them at the end
of the film. So the takeaway is that they

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:10.560
can have normal lives, but only when they’re
ready to stop being Avengers.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:13.519
Hawkeye only returns because it’s his ‘one
last mission’.

00:13:13.519 --> 00:13:20.519
Funny Side Note, Jeremy Renner still has movies
on his marvel contract. So
this isn’t the last time you’ll see hawkeye

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:59.190
in

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:09.320
a movie. He’ll probably cameo in Civil War.
But he won’t be an Avengers.

00:14:34.689 --> 00:14:41.689
The new Avengers as of the end of
the film are:
Captain America leading, Vision, Scarlet Witch,

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:37.600
who will

00:15:53.999 --> 00:16:00.999
probably hook up at some point, Falcon and
Black Widow.

